0..77 Comment "// A group\'s laws stated as rules, the coincidence check certifying each with"
78..156 Comment "// the others: the structure the circle\'s loops carry under composition, whose"
157..231 Comment "// laws `circle-group.gandr` proves as paths. The written laws do not join"
232..300 Comment "// among themselves: the cancellation `mul(inv(x), x) ==> e()` meets"
301..377 Comment "// associativity at `mul(mul(inv(x), x), z)`, which the two leave at `z` and"
378..455 Comment "// at `mul(inv(x), mul(x, z))`. Completion orients each such pair into a rule"
456..535 Comment "// that follows from the written ones, certified by the pair\'s two paths, until"
536..609 Comment "// every pair joins (Knuth and Bendix, _Simple Word Problems in Universal"
610..684 Comment "// Algebras_, 1970, § 7). The row reads a law no written rule states, the"
685..709 Comment "// inverse of a product."
710..712 Comment "//"
713..727 Comment "// - see: #338"
729..806 Comment "/// A group\'s unit, associativity and inverse laws, each a rule: `e()` is the"
807..885 Comment "/// unit and `a()`, `b()` two elements the row reads; the row\'s normal form is"
886..922 Comment "/// one only a derived rule reaches."
923..925 Other "@["
926..936 Other "normalizes"
936..937 Other "("
937..938 StringLit "\""
938..975 StringLit "inv(mul(a, b)) ~> mul(inv(b), inv(a))"
975..976 StringLit "\""
976..977 Other ")"
